From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 16:19:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: thermal: qcom,pas: add the CDSP HVX, HMX and HW
 TMD ids

The CDSP firmware of Kaanapali (SM8850) offers more thermal mitigation
devices over QMI TMD than "cdsp_sw" (the CDSP as a whole); on the
OnePlus Pad 4 it lists cdsp_hw, cdsp_sw, cdsp_sw_hvx, cdsp_sw_hmx,
cdsp_hw_hvx and cdsp_hw_hmx. The Pad 4's vendor kernel registers four
of them as cooling devices - cdsp_sw, the vector and matrix unit limits
cdsp_sw_hvx and cdsp_sw_hmx, and cdsp_hw (maximum levels 12, 11, 12
and 1) - and binds cdsp_sw_hvx to a PMIC temperature zone.

Add cooling-device ids for the three further endpoints it uses,
numbered after QCOM_TMD_CDSP_SW within the CDSP's own id space.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 include/dt-bindings/thermal/qcom,pas.h | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/dt-bindings/thermal/qcom,pas.h b/include/dt-bindings/thermal/qcom,pas.h
index f603bddef9a8..409666da1902 100644
--- a/include/dt-bindings/thermal/qcom,pas.h
+++ b/include/dt-bindings/thermal/qcom,pas.h
@@ -10,8 +10,11 @@
 #ifndef _DT_BINDINGS_THERMAL_QCOM_PAS_H
 #define _DT_BINDINGS_THERMAL_QCOM_PAS_H
 
-/* CDSP thermal mitigation device id */
+/* CDSP thermal mitigation device ids */
 #define QCOM_TMD_CDSP_SW	0
+#define QCOM_TMD_CDSP_SW_HVX	1
+#define QCOM_TMD_CDSP_SW_HMX	2
+#define QCOM_TMD_CDSP_HW	3
 
 /* Modem thermal mitigation device id */
 #define QCOM_TMD_PA	0
-- 
